  "review_notes": [
    "Corrected: the wherein unit at s022+s025 is now aligned rather than noncompositional. The chapter's other rule 30 fusions - therein at EZK.44.3 (s007+s008) and EZK.44.14 (s018+s019), theirs at EZK.44.29 (s017+s018) - are aligned, and the source difference between a relative and a suffix does not bear on whether the English word is indivisible. The corpus aligns the identical relative-plus-preposition-plus-suffix shape to wherein in twenty units.",
    "No edge and no head is changed by this patch. s026 remains unrepresented under rule 22, and the competing reading that folds it into the fusion, as those twenty corpus units do, is named in that unit's note under rule 8.",
